frankensim-shell-assembly-options-v1
# The existing il Cannone h8 body with an authored 20 micrometre exterior film.
# This is a modern measured oil/copal surrogate, NOT a reconstructed Guarneri
# or Stradivari recipe. Geometry, strings, bridge joints and pressure scale are
# unchanged. Source film conditioning: 293.15 K, RH 0.35.
window-hz 15 2000
projection-work 549755813888
reference-thickness-m 0.003
pack spruce @body
pack maple violin-maple-sycamore-sonderegger2013-shell.fsmatpk
# Coat all regions of explicitly exterior parts: top, back and ribs.
# Positive directors point outward in this table. No film is added to the
# bass bar, soundpost or bridge. Multiple rows would stack outward in order.
# Fields: component pack side h[m] reference[Hz] nu strain-limit RH storage-tolerance.
# nu=0.30 and strain-limit=0.001 are explicit modeling assumptions; they are
# not measured properties. Each retained body mode must satisfy <=25% relative
# storage drift from the reference slice. Modal loss uses the actual spectrum.
coating @exterior varnish-oil-copal-lammlein2021-s1.fsmatpk positive 0.000020 1000 0.30 0.001 0.35 0.25
bridge-component bridge
bridge-direction 1 0 0
bridge -0.01734 -0.05164
bridge -0.00557 -0.05421
bridge 0.00629 -0.05329
bridge 0.01728 -0.04887
